VS Code throws "Platform not supported" for process.platform === 'android'.
Treat Android like Linux: user data under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME or ~/.config.
Context checked against microsoft/vscode c4453f8e (the lib/vscode of code-server v4.145.2).

--- a/lib/vscode/src/vs/platform/environment/node/userDataPath.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/src/vs/platform/environment/node/userDataPath.ts
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
 		case 'linux':
+		case 'android':
 			appDataPath = process.env['XDG_CONFIG_HOME'] || join(homedir(), '.config');
 			break;
 		default:
 			throw new Error('Platform not supported');
 	}
